{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4538","id":4734371102,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU59Ms88AAAABGjDFHg","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4538","diff_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4538.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4538.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4538","number":4538,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SF-A13: fix Portable PDB compression errors and retain the original crash","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Task: SF-A29-T05.4\nRelated: #1146, #1151; follows #4531.\n\n## Observed defect and correction\nThe Portable PDB adapter found a malformed embedded-source stream that escaped the public reader as plain `Error: Reserved DEFLATE block`. The original observation was captured at published commit `ad0ea92f16bddcbcfecce884b93579fe94617c04`, tree `896f9233762f4d93de762b1325a4de9ca81c64d3`, before this fix.\n\nThe symbols decoder now translates only its 17 exact known plain-Error compression validations into SymbolError / SF_SYMBOL_INVALID_COMPRESSION. It retains the original error as a nonenumerable cause. Unexpected exception classes, names and messages still escape as findings; existing decoding and byte budgets are unchanged.\n\n## Original regression corpus\nPromote the original hash-named record unchanged into the normal A29 corpus. It retains literal input, source identity, observed budgets and the original finding. Its record digest is `3c86512192511f3ccac53a2a3524116a48c0db0347131bad5b81b86705213514`; input digest is `47aa8600a3eb7b339ac25d68ca91eecfabb45271d943899d875f84c05ffeb29f`. Replay now requires accepted or controlled-rejected behavior. The empty-corpus skip has become an executed passing regression for this record.\n\n## Changes outside A29\nMinimal A13 symbols error-contract fix with public API tests. Live A13 claim-ref lookup found no matching refs. The new test uses the existing a13-01-* manifest pattern. No archive runtime code or reserved owner files changed.\n\n## Validation\n- Parent public regressions: 2 failed, 1 passed before the correction.\n- Final: 12 tests passed, including public malformed compression, existing embedded compression, PDB boundary seeds and ordinary retained-corpus replay; no skips.\n- Command: `node scripts/limited.js node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-reporter=tap tests/a13-01-compression-errors.test.js tests/a13-01-embedded-compression.test.js tests/conformance/fuzz/portable-pdb-seed.test.js tests/conformance/fuzz/retained-corpus.test.js`.\n- Node 24.19.0, Linux x64; tested local commit `fab8efc873b386aef22d2b26af95c5121715ac4e`, tree `d22440892916ea69498210d8fc3ab7eee018d3ee`. Published tree verified identical; commit metadata differs.\n- Independent source and corpus byte-identity review passed; whitespace check passed.\n\nThis qualifies the recorded local cases, not the full affected-engine/platform matrix. No broader issue closure is claimed.","cre